# Build output.  parse.c in particular must never be committed: it is
# generated by yacc, and the bison skeleton it is built from carries the text
# of the GNU General Public License.  The exception in that skeleton does let
# the resulting parser stay permissive, but a file quoting the GPL in a tree
# whose whole point is licence hygiene is a finding waiting to happen - and
# the licence gate is meant to be run by a machine, which will not read the
# exception.
parse.c
*.o
cwm

tools/__pycache__/
